UID:10004864-1790168400-1790168400@jccmetrowest.org
SUMMARY:Life Long Learning: Mary Cassatt: Impressionist Painter and Printmaker with Janet Mandel
DESCRIPTION:In 2026\, not only are we celebrating the 250th anniversary of the birth of the USA\, but also the 100th anniversary of the death of artist Mary Cassatt. Janet Mandel will discuss how Cassatt\, the only American among the Impressionists\, has secured her place as a celebrated American icon. \nAbout the speaker: Janet Mandel retired after teaching for 32 years in the New Jersey public schools. She now presents illustrated lectures on art history at museums\, adult schools\, libraries\, and senior centers. \nFREE for JCC Member; $15 Nonmember\n \nRegister Here\n  \nSponsored by: \n \n  \nDAY TRIP \nOn Thursday\, October 15\, join us for a docent-led Impressionism and Beyond tour at the Philadelphia Museum of Art\, featuring seven Mary Cassatt paintings. The trip will include admission to the Marcel Duchamp retrospective as well\, a perfect complement to Janet’s March 2025 lecture.
URL:https://jccmetrowest.org/event/lll-mary-cassatt/
LOCATION:JCC MetroWest | Maurice Levin Theater\, 760 Northfield Ave\, West Orange\, NJ\, 07052\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Enrichment
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://jccmetrowest.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/LLL-Hero1-01.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Michele Bernstein":MAILTO:mbernstein@jccmetrowest.org
GEO:40.7674616;-74.2963088
